  "reviews": [
    {
      "body": "## Pull request overview\n\nThis PR optimizes GPU busy-time calculation in `TreePerfAnalyzer` by avoiding full `GPUEventAnalyser.compute_metrics()` execution when only `\"busy_time\"` is needed, reducing unnecessary categorization and metric computation work.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Added `GPUEventAnalyser.compute_busy_time()` to compute merged busy time directly from a kernel/event list.\n- Updated `TreePerfAnalyzer.compute_perf_metrics()` to use `compute_busy_time()` instead of `compute_metrics()[\"busy_time\"]`.\n- Removed redundant re-traversal for non-data-movement kernels by filtering the already-collected kernel list in-memory.\n\n### Reviewed changes\n\nCopilot reviewed 2 out of 2 changed files in this pull request and generated no comments.\n\n| File | Description |\n| ---- | ----------- |\n| TraceLens/TreePerf/tree_perf.py | Switches busy-time computations to the new direct busy-time helper and avoids a second kernel aggregation pass. |\n| TraceLens/TreePerf/gpu_event_analyser.py | Introduces a lightweight static helper to compute merged busy time without running full metric computation. |\n\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n\n💡 <a href=\"/AMD-AGI/TraceLens/new/main?filename=.github/instructions/*.instructions.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add Copilot custom instructions</a> for smarter, more guided reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/customizing-copilot/adding-repository-custom-instructions-for-github-copilot\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn how to get started</a>.",
